config CMD_TYPEWRITER
	bool "typewriter - Nano-like editor with Wubi Chinese input"
	depends on VIDEO
	depends on FS_FAT || FS_EXT4
	help
	  A full-screen, GNU Nano-style text editor that runs directly on
	  U-Boot's video framebuffer, with a built-in Wubi 86 (五笔) Chinese
	  input method. Chinese glyphs are drawn from an embedded GNU Unifont
	  subset; the Wubi table is embedded too, so no external files are
	  needed at runtime (this adds roughly 3 MB of read-only data to the
	  image, plus a few MB of BSS for the line buffer).

	  Requires a video display (CONFIG_VIDEO and a display driver) because
	  U-Boot's built-in console font is ASCII-only and cannot render hanzi.
	  Reads and writes UTF-8 files on FAT or ext4.

	  Use: typewriter <iftype> <dev:part> <filename> [fstype]
